  "environment_bible": "Build environments as sparse symbolic spaces rather than realistic rooms. Preferred settings include an off-white paper void, an abstract floor plane, a fading staircase or effort path, a distant opening, a large empty calendar with no readable dates or symbols, a looming smartphone-shaped black shadow without interface details, a simple hourglass, a rope leading toward a distant gold point, a cracked shell containing hidden effort strokes, and a threshold where visible results have not yet appeared. The recurring symbolic calendar must be shown as a mostly blank grid-like object with empty result areas and no numbers, letters, or labels; it represents the absence of visible feedback, not a factual data display. Objects should feel oversized when they represent psychological pressure and small when they represent the mascot's available agency. Keep spatial continuity through the same off-white paper field, black ink shadows, slate-blue clothing, and restrained gold signal. Use one dominant object or spatial metaphor per frame, never a collage. Maintain clear foreground, middle distance, and negative space, but avoid detailed architecture, desks, notebooks, classrooms, literal offices, realistic phones, or clutter. Any screen-like object must be a text-free black or simplified shape with no interface content.",
